# What `project/event_model.py`, `project/model_to_code.py`, `project/adversary.py` and
# `project/parallel_slices.py` rendered before the standing text in them moved out to `assets/`, as SHA-256
# over the UTF-8 bytes of each file.
#
# The move is only worth doing if it changed nothing a project receives, and "generate before and after"
# cannot be run across one commit. So these were captured at a6a0aed, the commit slice 16.5 was written on
# top of, by the matrix `tests/test_method_pages.py` describes, and the new path has to reproduce them
# exactly. Anyone can take the same reading: check out a6a0aed, put that module beside this file, and run
#
#     PYTHONPATH=src:tests python3 -c "import sys, test_method_pages; sys.stdout.write(test_method_pages.lines())"
#
# and compare it with the lines below. The module that prints them changes nothing the generator does, so
# the reading is the same whether it is taken at a6a0aed or at the commit that added it.
#
# Thirty-two combinations: four application sets — one service whose log is its truth, one that keeps
# current state, one of each, and no service at all — against both profiles, two destinations and both
# delivery layouts. `docs/first-slice.md`, `docs/event-modeling-to-code.md` and `docs/event-model/model.yaml`
# are written only on the event profile and only where the keel made a service, so eight combinations carry
# five files and the other twenty-four carry two.
#
# Two of the paths are no longer the a6a0aed reading. `commands/sail.md` and `docs/first-slice.md` were
# re-taken when the scheduling rules changed deliberately — two bands, a state per slice, refill at every
# boundary (`changelog.d/sail-scheduling-is-a-state.md`) — so their rows are what this checkout renders and
# the record holds them to that; the original reading of both is at 844b10c for anyone comparing against the
# move itself. Every other path is still the reading taken at a6a0aed.
#
# `<digest>  <apps>/<profile>/<target>/<delivery>  <path>`.
#
# Re-taken for the loop-cadence changes — review once per slice, a return is a commit, two concurrency
# numbers, the budget as work tokens, fast checks per deployable (`changelog.d/loop-cadence-*.md`).
# Only the rows named there moved: `commands/sail.md`. Every other row is still its earlier reading.
#
# Re-taken for the preflight run once per worktree (`changelog.d/loop-cadence-preflight-once-per-worktree.md`).
# Only the rows named there moved: `commands/sail.md`. Every other row is still its earlier reading.
#
# Re-taken for mutation once per capability, bounded (`changelog.d/loop-cadence-mutation-once-per-capability.md`).
# Only the rows named there moved: `commands/sail.md`. Every other row is still its earlier reading.
#
# Re-taken for the fairway priority (`changelog.d/18.2-the-streams-can-be-reordered.md`).
# Only the rows named there moved: `commands/sail.md`. Every other row is still its earlier reading.
# 2026-10-15: commands/sail.md moved deliberately — the ladder now runs `make arrive` beside its
# own fetch, `make dispatch` before any delegate, and `make depart` at every boundary, and the
# single-slice exit is a recorded probe rather than a judgement. Only those rows were re-taken.
# See changelog.d/the-loop-travels-and-says-what-it-dispatched.md.
# 2026-10-16: commands/sail.md moved deliberately — a further feature is handed to /sail in the
# conversation, captured, confirmed, and assessed before specify. Only those rows were re-taken.
# See changelog.d/a-further-feature-is-handed-to-sail.md.
# Re-taken for the profile staying put (changelog.d/a-further-feature-stays-on-this-profile.md).
# Only the rows named there moved: commands/assess.md, commands/draft.md, commands/sail.md.
# Every other row is still its earlier reading.
# Re-taken for the seam tests (changelog.d/a-seam-is-tested-three-ways.md): the context step on both
# profiles. Only the rows named there moved: commands/sail.md. Every other row is still its earlier reading.
#
# Re-taken for clarify, checklist and analyze (`changelog.d/clarify-checklist-and-analyze.md`).
# Only the rows named there moved: `commands/sail.md`. Every other row is still its earlier reading.
# Re-taken for the dispatch ledger's new home (`changelog.d/dispatch-ledger-moves-under-slipwai.md`).
# Only the rows named there moved: `commands/sail.md`. Every other row is still its earlier reading.
# Re-taken 2026-10-17 for changelog.d/capability-gates-once-per-capability.md: the rows for `commands/adversary.md`, `commands/sail.md` moved, deliberately — converge, gaps, design review, adversary, mutation and the hand's walk run once per capability, and three of them moved off the slice.
# Re-taken 2026-10-17 for changelog.d/a-slice-carries-its-own-dispatch-line.md: only the rows for commands/sail.md moved, deliberately — a slice's dispatch line travels in its own pull request, and a delegate hands the diff review it cannot start back to the host.
# Re-taken 2026-10-19 for changelog.d/the-context-decision-is-always-recorded.md: only the event-modelling rows for commands/sail.md moved, deliberately — the event model stage interrogates every stream before naming it and records the context answer, one context included, as a decision entry with its seam table.
# Re-taken 2026-10-19 for changelog.d/a-fairway-runs-its-ready-slices-abreast.md: only the rows for commands/sail.md moved, deliberately — the fleet honours rule 6 inside a fairway, a session the captain dispatched is already in its berth, and slices run abreast merge as each passes its gate.
